# TBD Reforger platform

- Read [`CLAUDE.md`](/CLAUDE.md) first: the project laws, the directory atlas and the canonical
  commands. Every path in the rules is relative to the repository root.
- **HARD GATE:** [`no-silent-deferrals.mdc`](/.cursor/rules/no-silent-deferrals.mdc) — finish the
  whole ask; only the operator's explicit "defer X" defers a piece.
- **HARD GATE:** [`cursor-agent-workflow.mdc`](/.cursor/rules/cursor-agent-workflow.mdc) — which
  mode a message asks for, and when to stop and ask.
- Layout: `apps/website/api_v2/` (Axum, package `website-api`) · `apps/website/frontend/` (Leptos
  and Trunk, package `website-frontend`) · `apps/website/map-engine/` (package
  `website-map-engine`) · `apps/website/graphics-engine/` (package `website-graphics-engine`) ·
  `apps/mod/` (the Enfusion addons). Where a new file goes:
  [Where does X go?](/documentation_v2/standards/where_does_x_go.md).
- **Documentation ships with its code.** A change updates, in the same commit, the comments of the
  code it alters, the README.md of every folder whose contents, surface, commands or boundaries it
  changes, and the feature docs whose behaviour it changes — whichever agent or person writes the
  code. Documentation lives in `documentation_v2/` (entry:
  [documentation_v2/README.md](/documentation_v2/README.md)); its rules are in
  [documentation_v2/standards/](/documentation_v2/standards/README.md): the
  [documentation standards](/documentation_v2/standards/documentation_standards.md), the
  [README standard](/documentation_v2/standards/readme_standard.md) and the
  [commit checklist](/documentation_v2/standards/commit_checklist.md). The code trees hold no
  Markdown but README.md files (`cargo xtask verify markdown-placement`, run by
  `cargo xtask ci verify-documentation`), so no application grows a documentation tree. Mission Creator documentation lives under
  [documentation_v2/website/frontend/apps/editor/](/documentation_v2/website/frontend/apps/editor/README.md).
- **Tickets.** One `.ai/tickets/T-<id>.toml` file per ticket, parent and child alike, beside the
  `.ai/tickets/ROOT` marker; the [ticket registry README](/.ai/tickets/README.md) lists the folder
  and the commands. A ticket file is created only by `cargo xtask ticket add` (or `add-child`); a
  hand edit keeps the ticket engine's canonical form; then run `cargo xtask ticket check --strict`.
  The whole lifecycle is
  [Taking a ticket from idea to shipped](/documentation_v2/runbooks/ticket_run_pipeline.md).
- **Executor gate.** A ticket's `executor` says who may take it: `claude-code` means any AI coding
  agent run through the ticket tooling, whoever makes it; `documentation` a ticket, spec or
  documentation pass; `workbench`, `human` and `ci` mean stop and wait for that party.
- **Git.** Commit directly to `main` and create no branch (`CLAUDE.md` law 2). The one exception
  is the `slice/<id>` branches that the xtask slice and wave tooling creates, merges and deletes
  itself (`cargo xtask platform slice-worktree`, `cargo xtask platform wave`,
  `cargo xtask mod wave`). A commit that lands a ticket names its id in the subject; a commit
  written with an AI agent ends with a `Co-Authored-By:` trailer; commit only when asked.
- **Factory mode.** When the operator starts the platform factory,
  [`platform-factory-mode.mdc`](/.cursor/rules/platform-factory-mode.mdc) applies and the
  orchestrating session follows
  [Factory waves](/documentation_v2/runbooks/factory_waves/README.md).
